---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { SITE } from '../site';

const updated = 'November 1, 2026';
---
<BaseLayout
  title="Privacy Policy"
  description="How this website handles visitor information. It does not use analytics, forms or advertising."
>
  <article class="wrap legal prose">
    <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
    <p class="project-meta">Last updated: {updated}</p>

    <p>
      This website is a portfolio for {SITE.name}. It is designed to collect as little
      information about you as possible.
    </p>

    <h2>What I collect</h2>
    <p>
      I do not run analytics, advertising, tracking tools or contact forms on this site, and
      I do not set cookies myself. I do not ask you to create an account or share personal
      details to browse it.
    </p>

    <h2>Email</h2>
    <p>
      If you email me at <a href={`mailto:${SITE.email}`}>{SITE.email}</a>, I receive your
      email address and whatever you choose to write. I use it only to reply to you, and I do
      not sell it or share it for marketing.
    </p>

    <h2>Hosting</h2>
    <p>
      The site is hosted by Cloudflare. Like most hosts, Cloudflare processes technical
      information when you visit, such as your IP address and browser type, to deliver the
      site and keep it secure. You can read how they handle it in
      <a href="https://www.cloudflare.com/privacypolicy/" rel="noopener">Cloudflare's privacy policy</a>.
    </p>

    <h2>Other websites</h2>
    <p>
      This site links to places like GitHub and LinkedIn, and to client websites. Those sites
      have their own privacy practices, which I do not control.
    </p>

    <h2>Changes</h2>
    <p>
      If I add tools such as analytics, I will update this page and the date above.
    </p>

    <h2>Contact</h2>
    <p>
      Questions about this policy? Email <a href={`mailto:${SITE.email}`}>{SITE.email}</a>.
    </p>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>